## D171 · 2026-10-25 · Review and free proofs for the day-batch acceleration proposal

- Alex asked to review the extraction/Jev/per-day acceleration plan deeply and test it against the stored golds and result databases. Scope is review and isolated offline proofs; no product-contract change, runtime adoption or paid comparison follows automatically.
- The [review](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/review.md) and its scripts reconstruct 960/960 extraction requests from the two saved v23 ledgers. Day-start context differs for 214/480 Jev-arm requests and 168/480 control requests; rechecking the same raw answers with day-start IDs loses 73/797 and 62/744 evidence items. Extraction depends on earlier theses as well as groups. The Jev arm has 86/320 final repeat/replace decisions targeting same-day evidence, and Jev membership alone cannot declare the 26 new groups.
- At 32 workers, a three-wave schedule using recorded Jev call durations projects 8.6× on July 27 and 3.2× over 31 nonempty days, before reconciliation/rate-limit overhead. This replaces the unsupported general 10× claim, not the speed target. It is a schedule estimate, not fresh measured latency. Judging already uses six workers per dependency level.
- Recommendation awaiting Alex's choice: concurrent request preparation with exact read validation before sequential commits, retaining D149/D159 semantics; re-run requests whose inputs changed. A more aggressive day-start extraction contract must be decided and tested separately. The review defines both boundaries, failure/recovery states, local-ID namespacing, evaluation limits and staged tests.
- Verification: 128 product/corpus/diagnostic tests passed; two diagnostic mutants were caught; preflight judged 250 stored Jev records with no skipped records. Existing golds remain unchanged. No batching runtime or fresh model-quality pass is claimed.
- A read-only review independently reproduced the 960 request message pairs and schemas, the stale-reference losses and the timing projection; no serious finding against the proposed contract. Runtime implementation and live measurement remain the next, separate steps.

## D172 · 2026-10-25 · Build the isolated ordered-concurrency POC

- Alex accepted the D171 recommendation: “yes be super careful about the logic ... do not fuck up the order ... flag it immediately”. Implement concurrent preparation with current-prefix validation and one ordered writer. Keep the default serial path and its tests unchanged. Group ownership and thesis/evidence semantics do not move.
- Speculative calls may precede earlier commits in the experimental path; accepted handovers and writes may not. Stale prepared requests are recomputed; earlier failure cancels pending work and drains running calls without accepting later results. This scheduling distinction is explicit, not an accidental weakening of D159.
- The [first implementation slice](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/implementation.md) covers offline coordinator, independent Jev calls and failure/restart verification on temporary storage. No paid call, new spending cap or default activation is authorized by this slice. The current per-item spend check is not safe reservation accounting for concurrent paid calls; resolve it before a live comparison.
- Offline slice result: [ordered-concurrency POC](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-concurrency-poc/results.md). Shared request identity prevents conflicting concurrent answers under one archive ID. Bounded Jev submission cancels pending work on failure; the daily cost log includes discarded speculative work. Default replay remains serial. 143 tests pass; five intended mutants fail; 3,595 historical request hashes are unchanged. Final focused review finds no serious issue. Live accounting, fresh controls and speed measurement remain outstanding; no paid ingestion calls were made.

## D173 · 2026-10-25 · Isolated provider smoke before a larger concurrency test

- Alex approved proceeding with a small test and required preserving the working database: “don't contaminate the current working db ... check the batch API usage correctly ... small scale test before moving forward”. All existing databases remain read-only; no merge or production activation is authorized.
- The [registered smoke](research/2026-10-25-api-smoke/plan.md) repeats two unchanged extraction requests and two unchanged Jev requests, with three fresh samples of two serial controls and one two-worker arm. Maximum 36 requests; conservative $1.50 reservation ceiling; no automatic retries. This is ordinary API concurrency, not OpenAI's asynchronous Batch API, and is not end-to-end or 10x acceptance.
- The isolated transport reserves money before dispatch, retains unknown usage after failures, and closes admission on any worker failure or cancellation. A synchronized dispatch decision separates work not yet committed to sending from in-flight work. The provider endpoints, pinned models, response shapes and price envelopes were checked against the official documentation. Existing prompts, product behavior, golds and default transports remain unchanged.
- Result: [36-request smoke](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-api-smoke/results.md) completed with valid responses, no retries, and all 122 pre-existing database files unchanged. Median two-request speed ratios were 1.08x extraction and 1.77x Jev. Fresh extraction varied between controls; one of 27 Jev categorical comparisons differed. This passes API integration, not semantic or 10x acceptance. A small end-to-end comparison remains next; no production promotion.
def check_schema(value, schema, path='$'):
    """A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,
    array/items, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf."""
    kind = schema.get('type')
    if 'anyOf' in schema:
        errors = []
        for option in schema['anyOf']:
            errors = check_schema(value, option, path)
            if not errors:
                return []
        return errors or [f'{path}: matches no option']
    if kind == 'object':
        if not isinstance(value, dict):
            return [f'{path}: expected object']
        errors = []
        for name in schema.get('required', []):
            if name not in value:
                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: required')
        properties = schema.get('properties', {})
        for name, item in value.items():
            if name in properties:
                errors.extend(check_schema(item, properties[name], f'{path}.{name}'))
            elif schema.get('additionalProperties') is False:
                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: not allowed')
        return errors
    if kind == 'array':
        if not isinstance(value, list):
            return [f'{path}: expected array']
        errors = []
        for index, item in enumerate(value):
            errors.extend(check_schema(item, schema.get('items', {}), f'{path}[{index}]'))
        return errors
    if kind == 'string':
        if not isinstance(value, str):
            return [f'{path}: expected string']
        if 'enum' in schema and value not in schema['enum']:
            return [f'{path}: {value!r} not in {schema["enum"]}']
        if 'pattern' in schema and not re.search(schema['pattern'], value):
            return [f'{path}: {value!r} does not match {schema["pattern"]}']
        return []
    if kind == 'integer':
        return [] if isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected integer']
    if kind == 'number':
        return [] if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected number']
    if kind == 'boolean':
        return [] if isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected boolean']
    if kind == 'null':
        return [] if value is None else [f'{path}: expected null']
    return []


def request_identity(request):
    """The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation."""
    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)
    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()


def call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):
    provider = cfg.provider
    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)
    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)
    hit = archive.lookup(sha)
    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)
    if hit:
        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit
        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)
    started = time.time()
    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)
    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)
    try:
        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']
        data = json.loads(content)
    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:
        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,
                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,
                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,
                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))
        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')
    errors = check_schema(data, schema)
    usage = response.get('usage') or {}
    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)
    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)
    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))
    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)
    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,
                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,
                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),
                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,
                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))
    if errors:
        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))
    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)
def check_answer(conn, view_id, data):
    errors = []
    in_force = {p['evidence_id'] for p in store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)}
    deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}
    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)
    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):
        errors.append(f'rung {data["rung"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')
    for cited in data['cites']:
        if cited not in in_force:
            errors.append(f'{cited} is not evidence in force under {view_id}' + (' (replaced)' if store.is_replaced(conn, cited) else ''))
    for cited in data['cites_views']:
        if cited not in deps:
            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')
    for push in data['pushes']:
        if push['evidence_id'] not in in_force:
            errors.append(f'push on {push["evidence_id"]} which is not under {view_id}')
    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)
    if last is None and not data['changed']:
        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')
    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:
        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last["rung"]} to {data["rung"]} but changed is false')
    return errors


def _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):
    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)
    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],
                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),
                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,
                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,
                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])
    conn.commit()
    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}


JUDGE_WORKERS = 6


def upstream(conn, view_id):
    """Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies."""
    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]
    while stack:
        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):
            target = dep['resolved_to']
            if target and target not in seen:
                seen.add(target)
                stack.append(target)
    return seen


def round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):
    """Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.

    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent
    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the
    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a
    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays
    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice."""
    import concurrent.futures

    schema = schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version)

    def eligible(view_id):
        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))

    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, changed_views) if eligible(v)]
    done, results = set(), []
    while pending:
        level = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]
        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, cfg.rejudging.prompt_version) for v in level}

        def ask(view_id, note=''):
            system, user = prompts[view_id]
            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)

        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:
            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))
        for view_id in level:
            answer = answers[view_id]
            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data)
            if errors:
                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version, errors))
                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data)
                if errors:
                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))
            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)
            done.add(view_id)
            results.append(result)
            if result['changed']:
                for dependant in store.dependants_of(conn, view_id):
                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):
                        pending.append(dependant)
        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]
    return results

